// Shield counters ([CR#122.1c]): one or more create a single replacement
// effect ("if this permanent would be destroyed, instead remove a shield
// counter from it") and a single prevention effect ("if damage would be dealt
// to this permanent, prevent it and remove a shield counter") — [CR#614]
// (Replacement Effects) and [CR#615] (Prevention Effects). This is a bare
// MARKER decl, like `AgeCounter`/`LoyaltyCounter`: it lets the counter be
// placed and counted (`enters-with-counters` [CR#122.6a]); the shield's own
// destroy-replacement/damage-prevention behavior is a separate, unbuilt
// feature (no `confers` entry here yet).
CounterKind(
    name: "ShieldCounter",
    params: [],
    spelling: "shield",
    grammar: FixedTerm(surface: "shield"),
    body: Counter(name: "ShieldCounter"),
)
